From 1fbb786e6e92af9d903046c65bb73dea19a10387 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 11:36:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wm8994: add a prompt to allow defconfig
 selection

SND_SOC_WM8994 is currently declared as a tristate without any prompt.
That makes it a non-visible Kconfig symbol, so it cannot be selected
directly from a defconfig fragment even when its dependency
MFD_WM8994 is enabled.

On STM32 platforms, the codec is requested from the addon config
fragment, but the value is dropped during Kconfig resolution because
the symbol is hidden. Adding a prompt makes the option user-visible
and allows the requested defconfig value to be preserved.

This change does not alter runtime behavior or dependencies. It only
makes the wm8994 codec selectable through standard configuration flows
such as defconfig fragments and menuconfig.

Change-Id: Iaf5cddb0d0af22730a8c564c19e8645ed17ef545
Signed-off-by: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/562137
Reviewed-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig
@@ -2570,7 +2570,7 @@ config SND_SOC_WM8993
 	depends on I2C
 
 config SND_SOC_WM8994
-	tristate
+	tristate "Wolfson Microelectronics WM8994 codec"
 	depends on MFD_WM8994
 
 config SND_SOC_WM8995
